INTERVIEW TRAP QUESTIONS
======================================================================

Trap 1

Question

What is the official definition of SRP?

Correct Answer

"A class should have only one responsibility
or one reason to change."

---------------------------------------------------------------------

Trap 2

Question

Does SRP mean one class should contain only one method?

Correct Answer

No.

A class can have many methods as long as
they all belong to the same responsibility.

---------------------------------------------------------------------

Trap 3

Question

Can a class with 20 methods still follow SRP?

Correct Answer

Yes.

If all methods contribute to one responsibility,
SRP is satisfied.

---------------------------------------------------------------------

Trap 4

Question

Does SRP reduce the number of classes?

Correct Answer

No.

SRP often increases the number of classes,
but each class becomes smaller,
more maintainable,
and easier to test.

---------------------------------------------------------------------

Trap 5

Question

What happens if SRP is violated?

Correct Answer

• Difficult Maintenance.
• Difficult Testing.
• High Coupling.
• More Bugs.
• Lower Reusability.

---------------------------------------------------------------------

Trap 6

Question

How do you identify an SRP violation?

Correct Answer

Ask this question:

"Does this class have more than one reason to change?"

If YES,

SRP is violated.

---------------------------------------------------------------------

Trap 7

Question

Can multiple methods exist in one class
without violating SRP?

Correct Answer

Yes.

As long as all methods belong to
the same responsibility.

Example

BankAccount

deposit()

withdraw()

getBalance()

All belong to Bank Account Management.

